Problem - Middle of the Linked List( 876)

Aim-Given the head of a singly linked list, return the middle node of the linked list.

Algorithm-
Initialize two pointers: slow and fast, both pointing to head.
Move slow one node at a time.
Move fast two nodes at a time.
Continue while fast and fast.next are not None.
When the loop ends, slow will point to the middle node.
Return slow.
For an even-sized list, slow reaches the second middle node.

Code- 
class Solution(object):
    def middleNode(self, head):
        slow = head
        fast = head

        while fast and fast.next:
            slow = slow.next
            fast = fast.next.next

        return slow
